# drafting-manuscript gate overrides

2026-10-12 — SoK manuscript, target manuscript/sok.qmd
  Unmet: (1) no knowledge/synthesis tree, (3) no wiki/lint-wiki.py,
         (4) no <slug>-plan.md with an explicit Draft task,
         (5) no review_flags mechanism.
  Reason: the skill assumes a Quarto research-project template with a
  per-source wiki. This project predates it and stores the equivalent content
  differently: 28 regenerable result documents in the repo root play the role
  of stable synthesis pages (each carries measured results, a regeneration
  script, and a dated revision history including corrections), and the corpus
  lives in SQLite rather than as per-source pages. Scaffolding a wiki around
  finished work would not add verification, only indirection.
  Gate (2) was NOT overridden - it was closed: manuscript/references.bib is
  generated from the 1158-paper corpus by scripts/build_bibtex.py, and every
  bibkey the manuscript needs resolves.
  Stops NOT skipped: STOP 1, 2 and 3 are being honoured.

  Substantive caveat carried into the draft: the corpus coding is an
  LLM-assisted extraction pass that no human has verified (see
  CONTRIBUTOR_BRIEF.md). This is the moral equivalent of an open review_flag
  on every source page, and it constrains what the manuscript may claim. Every
  count derived from the coding is reported as provisional pending the
  verification pass, and the Limitations section states this rather than
  burying it.
